@prefix ds: <https://ds.canonical.com/>.
@prefix anatomy: <https://anatomy.canonical.com/>.
@prefix dt: <https://dt.canonical.com/>.

ds:apps_landscape.component.tag_multi_select a ds:Component;
    ds:name "Tag Multi-Select";
    ds:summary "A Landscape-specific controlled field for adding and removing instance tags. It fetches available tags via `useGetTags`, displays selected tags as dismissible Chips, filters unselected tags by case-insensitive substring, and validates typed new tags against a naming pattern before appending.\n\nMain use cases:\n\n- Assign and modify tags for Landscape instances in create/edit workflows.  \n- Allow users to discover existing tags through server-backed search or create conforming new tags inline.";
    ds:anatomyDsl "node:\n  uri: ds:apps_landscape.component.tag_multi_select\n  role: Landscape instance-tag field\n  edges:\n    - node:\n        semantic: label\n        role: field label\n        relation:\n          cardinality: \"1\"\n    - node:\n        role: owning search and filter wrapper\n        edges:\n          - node:\n              role: search container\n              edges:\n                - node:\n                    uri: global.component.chip\n                    role: selected tag\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"0..*\"\n                - node:\n                    uri: global.component.input\n                    role: search or create tag\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"1\"\n                - node:\n                    role: validation message\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                      condition: inputError is truthy\n                - node:\n                    role: overflow info\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                      condition: overflowingChipsAmount is greater than zero and dropdown is closed\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"1\"\n          - node:\n              role: loading state\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                condition: dropdown is open and tag query is pending\n          - node:\n              role: dropdown panel\n              edges:\n                - node:\n                    role: create prompt\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                      condition: inputText is non-empty\n                - node:\n                    role: matching tag list\n                    edges:\n                      - node:\n                          semantic: p\n                          role: tag list heading\n                          relation:\n                            cardinality: \"1\"\n                      - node:\n                          semantic: ul\n                          role: tag results\n                          edges:\n                            - node:\n                                semantic: li\n                                role: tag result\n                                edges:\n                                  - node:\n                                      uri: global.component.button\n                                      role: select existing tag\n                                      relation:\n                                        cardinality: \"1\"\n                                relation:\n                                  cardinality: \"1..*\"\n                          relation:\n                            cardinality: \"1\"\n                    relation:\n                      cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                      condition: filteredTags contains at least one tag\n              relation:\n                cardinality: \"0..1\"\n                condition: dropdown is open and tag query is not pending\n        relation:\n          cardinality: \"1\"";
    ds:anatomyClassic "https://www.figma.com/design/I4WpvwMuQI6v1qhgUl63Sx/Landscape-Pragma-components?node-id=26-13&t=iG2ObZ6Q1XG2A2MB-4\n\nTable 70\n\nThe owning wrapper uses `p-search-and-filter`, the search container uses `p-search-and-filter__search-container`, and the dropdown panel uses `p-search-and-filter__panel`.";
    ds:usage "### When to use\n\n**Landscape tag assignment**\n\nUse when editing controlled instance tags backed by the Landscape tags endpoint.\n\n**Validated tag creation**\n\nUse when the owning workflow allows appending a new tag string that starts with an ASCII letter and otherwise contains ASCII letters, digits, hyphens, or underscores.\n\n### When not to use\n\n**Generic multi-select lists**\n\nSelecting from arbitrary option arrays instead of Landscape tag management.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Using TagMultiSelect for non-tag categories (projects, profiles, environments) that don’t require server tag fetching.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Implement a dedicated multi-select component using React Query and your own option array. Reserve TagMultiSelect for Landscape instance tags only.\n\n**Tag taxonomy administration**\n\nRenaming, deleting, or organizing the tag system itself.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Using TagMultiSelect as the interface for tag creation, modification, or deletion workflows.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Implement separate admin forms or pages for tag management. TagMultiSelect is a field-level selector only, not an admin interface.\n\n**Accessibility-critical multiselect combobox**\n\nApplications where robust ARIA combobox semantics and full keyboard navigation are required.\n\n**Incorrect pattern**: Treating the current implementation as a complete ARIA multi-select combobox with full keyboard support and announced states.\n\n**Remediation strategy**: Implement or adopt an accessible combobox component with explicit `role=\"combobox\"`, active-descendant focus management, and all ARIA live-region announcements. The current TagMultiSelect needs semantic work before WCAG AA compliance can be claimed.";
    ds:guidelines "### Accessibility\n\n- Current source needs an interactive combobox owner with `aria-expanded`, `aria-controls`, listbox/option semantics, active-descendant or roving focus, and selected states before upstream adoption.\n- Canonical Chip supplies dismiss controls, but local tests find each by the generic name “Dismiss”; tag-specific naming is not proven.\n- Input error uses `aria-invalid` and conditional `aria-errormessage`. Its id depends on an input id discovered after mount; before discovery it can be `-error`. Stability and screen-reader behavior are not covered by tests.\n- Label association also depends on post-mount DOM discovery rather than a caller/generated id contract.\n- No live region announces loading, result count, selection, removal, creation, closure, or overflow changes.\n\n### Content\n\n- “Tags”, “Add tags”, “Search for”, “Add tag”, list heading “Tags”, “Error:”, and validation messages are hardcoded English with no translation props except `label`.\n- The create prompt does not explicitly distinguish a new tag from a search, and it remains available for text matching an existing tag.\n- Correct “Tag must starts with a letter” before treating the component as content-ready.\n- Validation is ASCII-specific and does not accept letters from other scripts.\n\n### Keyboard and device\n\n- Input `keyup` behavior: Enter opens when closed; Enter creates when open; Escape closes when open. It does not prevent default form submission in this handler.\n- Existing-result buttons require Tab traversal or pointer activation; Arrow Up/Down, Home/End, active option, and Enter-to-select-result are absent.\n- Clicking anywhere in the search container opens the panel, including chip interactions before event propagation completes; outside click closes it.\n- Focus is not moved on open/close, after creation, or after dismissal.\n\n### State, query, and validation behavior\n\n- `useGetTags` uses React Query key `instanceTags`, authenticated fetch of `tags`, empty-array fallback, and `isPending` as loading. The component has no query error or retry message.\n- Filtering removes values present in controlled `tags` and performs trimmed, case-insensitive substring matching. With no input and no selected tags, it returns the fetched array unchanged.\n- Clicking an existing result appends it but does not locally clear input or close the panel. Creation appends trimmed text, clears input/error, and disables change-time validation after success.\n- Invalid creation retains text, stores the thrown Yup message, and enables validation on subsequent changes. Non-`Error` throws are ignored.\n- The component has no disabled, read-only, submission-loading, mutation, or server-side tag-creation state.\n\n### Device / layout\n\n- Root bottom margin is `2.5 * $sp-unit`; input flex basis is `8rem`; search container and box use `!important` padding/margin calculations based on Vanilla icon sizes and `$bar-thickness`.\n- Result list has `max-height: 20rem` and vertical scrolling. Prompt text is single-line ellipsized while Add tag does not shrink.\n- Panel placement compares available viewport height with a hardcoded `379` pixel estimate. It sets inline `top: 100%; bottom: auto` or the inverse and recomputes when open, window height changes, or measured chip-container height changes.\n- Placement does not account for panel’s actual rendered height, horizontal viewport bounds, window width, scrolling ancestors, or virtual keyboard. There are no component breakpoints.\n- Overflow count uses chip `offsetTop > offsetHeight`, recalculated on window resize and when tag count changes; it is a heuristic and is not recomputed for every font/layout change.";
    ds:tier ds:apps_landscape;
    ds:documentationStage ds:tag.specialadoption-docs;
    ds:hasProperty [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`tags`";
        ds:summary "Supplies controlled tag names rendered as chips and excluded from fetched results. ";
        ds:propertyType "list of text";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "TypeScript: `string[]`. Source does not deduplicate. Dismiss removes all equal strings; add appends even if the value already exists. Creation trims before validation and append. Internal Yup `validationSchema` is neither a prop nor a top-level export: it requires `^[a-zA-Z]`, then `^[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9_-]*$`. Its first error is `Tag must starts with a letter`. After an initial failure, change-time validation uses untrimmed input while creation validates trimmed input. "
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`onTagsChange`";
        ds:summary "Receives the full next selection after add, create, or dismiss. ";
        ds:propertyType "callback";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "TypeScript: `(value: string[]) => void`. Consumer must update `tags`; no optimistic local selection state exists. "
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`label`";
        ds:summary "Supplies visible label text.";
        ds:propertyType "text";
        ds:defaultValue "`Tags`";
        ds:constraints "TypeScript: `string`. Falsy values fall back to `Tags` because the source uses a logical-OR fallback. ";
        ds:optional "true"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`labelClassName`";
        ds:summary "Adds a label class.";
        ds:propertyType "text";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "TypeScript: `string`. Combined with `p-form__label` and the optional required class. ";
        ds:optional "true"
    ], [
        a ds:Property;
        ds:name "`required`";
        ds:summary "Adds `is-required` to the label.";
        ds:propertyType "boolean";
        ds:defaultValue "—";
        ds:constraints "TypeScript: `boolean`. Does not validate selection count or set an input `required` attribute. ";
        ds:optional "true"
    ].
